# EDW start menu

When the user's message is only (or primarily) one of: `start`, `menu`, `help`, `hi`, `hello`:

1. Follow **`edw-start`** (`agents/prompts/06_start.md` / `.cursor/agents/edw-start.md`).
2. Run `./agents/tools/start_status.sh`, summarize briefly (mention `CURRENT_RUN` if present), print the numbered phrase menu, and **stop**.
3. Do **not** run Track A preflight, `make bootstrap`, or `make setup` until they pick menu item **1**, **2**, or **3** (or paste that phrase).

After they choose a number or phrase, route as `edw-start` specifies (demo-guide, coordinator, print-urls, teardown, or enterprise docs).
